 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": 99,
   "type": "Note",
   "title": "How to use",
   "pos": [
    -420,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    400,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "GRUNGO ADJUST (blorbarium art/comfy, see README.md)\n\nFirst time: uv run --with pillow --with numpy python art/comfy/run.py install\nThat uploads grungo_<frame>.png, grungo_mask_<preset>.png and grungo_alpha.png.\n\n1. Input frame: pick grungo_<frame>.png. To edit your own area, right-click it > Open in MaskEditor and paint; the strokes add to the preset.\n2. Mask preset: face / facebox / eyes / mouth / body / canvas / none (paint-only).\n3. Write the change in the positive prompt between the subject and the style.\n4. Denoise: 0.4 subtle, 0.6 reshapes, 0.8-0.9 redraws the masked area.\n5. Queue. 'Adjusted frame' keeps every pixel outside the mask and the anchor alpha, so it drops into pets/grungo/art/frames.\nNew silhouettes (a pose): preset canvas, then save 'Raw decode' instead; it is not clipped to the body."
   ]
  },
